.TH CREATE-ENVIRONMENT.SH 1 "2026-09-10" "mu2edaq-shifter-tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
create-environment.sh \- create or update a DAQ spack test release
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B create-environment.sh
[\fB\-c\fR \fIconfig\fR]
[\fB\-z\fR \fIpartition\fR]
\fB\-e\fR \fIenvironment\fR
[\fB\-u\fR]
[\fB\-b\fR \fIref\fR]
[\fB\-n\fR]
[\fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B create-environment.sh
materialises the spack test release that one DAQ environment needs.
The target directory is the environment's \fBtest_rel_path\fR in the
operations YAML.
.PP
If that directory does not exist, the script creates it, downloads
\fBmu2e\-quick\-spack\-start.sh\fR from the \fBMu2e/otsdaq\-mu2e\fR
repository, and runs it with \fB\-\-develop \-\-upstream\fR pointed at
the partition's \fBbase_release\fR.
.PP
If the directory already exists, the helper already inside it is re-run
with \fB\-\-develop\fR to update the release in place. A directory that
exists but has no helper in it is reported as an error rather than
being re-populated, since that usually means a partial or hand-made
release; remove it to have it rebuilt.
.SH OPTIONS
Configuration precedence is command line, then environment variable,
then .env file, then config file, then built-in default.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Operations YAML to read. Environment: \fBMU2EDAQ_CONFIG\fR.
.TP
.BR \-z ", " \-\-partition " " \fINAME\fR
Partition owning the environment. Environment:
\fBMU2EDAQ_PARTITION\fR. Default: \fIpartition_0\fR.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-environment " " \fINAME\fR
Environment to create. Required. Environment:
\fBMU2EDAQ_ENVIRONMENT\fR.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-update\-only
Refuse to create a missing test release; only update an existing one.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-branch " " \fIREF\fR
Git ref of \fBMu2e/otsdaq\-mu2e\fR to fetch the spack quick-start
helper from. Environment: \fBMU2EDAQ_OTSDAQ_REF\fR. Default:
\fIdevelop\fR.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print the commands that would run and change nothing.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Trace execution with \fBset \-x\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CREATE_ENVIRONMENT_SH_OPTS
Extra options, prepended to the command line.
.SH NOTES
Building a release takes a long time and needs network access to
GitHub and to the spack upstream. Run it before a shift, not during
one.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The release was created or updated, or the dry run completed.
.TP
.B 1
The configuration could not be read, no \fBtest_rel_path\fR or
\fBbase_release\fR is configured, the directory is missing under
\fB\-\-update\-only\fR, or the download or spack helper failed.
.TP
.B 2
An environment was not given, or an option was not recognised.
.SH EXAMPLES
Create the tracker test release:
.PP
.RS
.nf
create-environment.sh -z partition_0 -e tracker
.fi
.RE
.PP
Update it later without ever creating one:
.PP
.RS
.nf
create-environment.sh -z partition_0 -e tracker --update-only
.fi
.RE
.PP
Build against a branch of otsdaq-mu2e:
.PP
.RS
.nf
create-environment.sh -z partition_0 -e tracker -b my-feature-branch
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR setup-online.sh (1),
.BR start-daq.sh (1),
.BR daq-read-config (1),
.BR daq-install-tools (1)
